      "correctAnswer": "(u / 2) √5",
      "solution": "Displacement to highest point: x = u cos θ * (u sin θ / g) = u² / (2g), y = u² sin² θ / (2g) = u² / (4g). Net displacement S = √(x² + y²) = (u²/g) √(1/4 + 1/16) = (u²/g) (√5 / 4). Time to highest point t = u sin θ / g = u / (√2 g). Average velocity = S / t = [ (u²/g)(√5/4) ] / [ u / (√2 g) ] = (u √5 √2) / 4 = (u √10) / 4 = u √(5/8) = (u/2)√(5/2). For θ=45°, v_avg = (u/2)√5.",
